[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tvofi/heatpump_optimizer/pulls/2203","id":4857585501,"node_id":"PR_kwDOT-9fds8AAAABIYjfXQ","html_url":"https://github.com/tvofi/heatpump_optimizer/pull/2203","diff_url":"https://github.com/tvofi/heatpump_optimizer/pull/2203.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/tvofi/heatpump_optimizer/pull/2203.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tvofi/heatpump_optimizer/issues/2203","number":2203,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"fix(record-autofix): keep the --require-green call a condition so bash -e cannot abort the merge step","user":{"login":"hpo-author[bot]","id":331381602,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOE8B7Yg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70032254?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpo-author%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/hpo-author","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpo-author%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpo-author%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpo-author%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpo-author%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpo-author%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpo-author%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpo-author%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpo-author%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpo-author%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"The record-autofix beat's merge step ends the STEP, not just the merge, on any\nnon-green automerge-guard exit — so main ran red on every pending or refused\nbeat.\n\n`record-autofix` is red on `main` today (run 38553291314: `fast`+`closures`\nSUCCESS, `record-autofix` FAILURE; the merge step exits 3). The brief framed\nthis as a #2196 regression — the roster move to `dev/programme/rosters/` and\n`ROSTER_REF=main`. It is not. The step failed the same way at 04:58, 05:28,\n06:03, 07:43 and 08:35 on 2026-10-14, every one of them BEFORE #2196 merged at\n10:15; and on the failing run the automerge guard PASSED (`AUTOMERGE OK #2202`)\n— the roster read works, so no guard refusal is in play.\n\nThe cause is the step's shell. GitHub runs a `run:` block under `bash -e`. The\nstep called `guard --require-green; rc=$?` as a BARE command, so a non-zero\nguard exit ended the STEP right there — with 3 while a required check still\nruns, 1 on a refusal — before the `case` after it could turn either into\n`say ...; exit 0`. The graceful branches have produced no output since #2029\n(2026-10-07). The step's own comment states the contract it was breaking:\n\"Every outcome here is green; the report step reddens a beat that did not land.\"\n\nThe fix wraps the call in a condition, which `-e` exempts:\n\n```\nif guard --require-green; then rc=0; else rc=$?; fi\n```\n\nThe exit now reaches the `case`: a pending beat greens the job and waits (its\nreview is kept), a refusal dismisses the bot's review and keeps the manual one.\nNothing about the guard's exit codes, the review gate or the head-pinned merge\nchanges.\n\n## Head\n\nbc2ad696444935caadfb1d346eecefb067e28e42\n\n## Mutation proof\n\nThe pin added to `tests/entities.py` refuses the buggy wiring. Break the fix —\nrestore the bare `guard --require-green; rc=$?` into `.github/workflows/\ntests.yml` — and `python3 tests/entities.py` reports `1 of 2303 ENTITY CHECKS\nFAILED`, the single failure being\n\n    FAIL tests.yml's record-autofix job: main-only, its own environment, loop-guarded ci: subject, guarded write set\n\n(`_raf_merge_pinned`, one conjunct of `_raf_job_ok`, rejects a `guard\n--require-green` at line start and requires the condition form). The same break\nunder `bash -e -c '<step body>'` with `guard(){ return 3; }` ends the STEP with\nexit 3 and no `case` output — the CI signature, a step log whose last line is\n`Process completed with exit code 3`.\n\n## Null control\n\nThe unmodified tree does both. `git show origin/main:.github/workflows/\ntests.yml`'s step, run as the workflow does, exits 3 on a pending guard — run\n38553291314's automerge step, whose log has no `AUTOMERGE:` line because it\nnever reached `say`. And `python3 tests/entities.py` over the unmodified job\nturns the new pin red, the `1 of 2303` above; with the fix all `2303` pass.\n\n## Figures\n\none line per figure the body states, with the command that printed it:\n\n- `gh run view 38553291314 --log` — the automerge step's exit 3 with no\n  `AUTOMERGE:` line.\n- `PYTHONPATH=\"$PWD/tests/hastub\" python3 tests/entities.py` — `1 of 2303`\n  against the bare call, `ALL 2303 ENTITY CHECKS PASSED` against the fix; the\n  `record-autofix` pin is `_raf_job_ok`.\n- `python3 tests/structure.py` — `STRUCTURE RATCHET PASSED`, every metric `<=`\n  its `structure_budgets.json` value.\n\n## Red checks\n\n- `record-autofix` — this pull request's own subject. The step exits non-zero\n  under `bash -e` on a pending (3) or refused (1) guard result and reddens the\n  job the report step is meant to decide. Cheaper detector: the\n  `_raf_merge_pinned` pin added here, which runs in the `fast` lane's\n  `tests/entities.py` and rejects a bare `guard --require-green` from a few\n  milliseconds of regex over the job text, against the record-autofix job's\n  own run on `main`. Before this pin the cheapest detector that would have\n  caught it WAS the gate that did — no cheaper one existed.\n- `nightly-status` — red as `main`'s, not this head's. The last scheduled run\n  (38530020347) failed its `slow` lane, and this diff touches\n  `.github/workflows/tests.yml`, a reporter input, so the exemption is void and\n  it must be named. `tests/nightly_status.py` is CI's detector and it runs on\n  every pull request (its own runtime); no cheaper local one exists. Clearing it\n  is the orchestrator's, on `main` (`defect-root-cause.md`).\n\n## Forward-carry\n\nnone\n\n## Friction\n\nnone\n","created_at":"2026-10-14T12:05:27Z","updated_at":"2026-10-14T12:40:00Z","closed_at":"2026-10-14T12:39:57Z","merged_at":"2026-10-14T12:39:57Z","merge_commit_sha":"686126772de473184730f909a1483f81a4cdc2c4","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":false,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tvofi/heatpump_optimizer/pulls/2203/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tvofi/heatpump_optimizer/pulls/2203/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tvofi/heatpump_optimizer/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tvofi/heatpump_optimizer/issues/2203/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tvofi/heatpump_optimizer/statuses/bc2ad696444935caadfb1d346eecefb067e28e42","head":{"label":"tvofi:fix/record-automerge-regression","ref":"fix/record-automerge-regression","sha":"bc2ad696444935caadfb1d346eecefb067e28e42","user":{"login":"tvofi","id":70032254,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcwMDMyMjU0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70032254?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tvofi","html_url":"https://github.com/tvofi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tvofi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tvofi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tvofi/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tvofi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tvofi/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tvofi/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tvofi/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tvofi/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tvofi/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"repo":{"id":1341087606,"node_id":"R_kgDO